  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African elephant conservation genetics: GIS mapping of haplotypes for ivory forensics</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Geneticists have tried to identify the geographic region of origin of ivory using genetic markers. Recent developments using mitochondrial DNA (mtDNA) show great promise in identifying geographic origin more reliably than previous methods. This project will refine the method for mapping mtDNA to source sites using existing reference samples, collect additional samples from unsampled sites, and will develop a system and conduct training to make this technique and technology accessible and usable in African range states and wherever seizures occur.</narrative>
  </description>
